      "content": "While displaying an exact quota, like 3 products left, may be attention-grabbing, it can indeed lead to buyer's remorse or frustration if the product becomes available later that day. Consider striking a balance by using a tiered scarcity strategy: display a rough estimate (e.g., \"only a handful left\") or a short span (e.g., \"until tonight\") to convey a sense of urgency without making unrealistic promises.",
